    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1025">

                <pb facs="1283" n="1269" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg1269"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811F.244/6–245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Donnelly</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panamá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-02T19:00:00-05:00">June 2, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>533. See Emb despatch 1770 of May 22, 1945.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1025-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">La Estrella De Panama</hi> today reported that the Canal
                    Zone authorities have issued an order limiting the gold commissary purchase
                        privilege<anchor n="4" xml:id="d1025-f2"/> to [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >of</hi>] alien civilian employees to $50 per month if single and $100 per
                    month if married.</p>
                <p>The order which became effective on June 1 will result in complaints here on the
                    grounds of discrimination in the treatment of US and Panamanian civilian
                    employees. In fact the FonOff today called me there to discuss the matter. I
                    have exchanged views with the Governor of the Panama Canal and at my suggestion
                    a meeting will be held next week of representatives of the FonOff, the Embassy
                    and the Panama Canal when we will endeavor to arrive at a satisfactory solution
                    of the problem especially the charge of discrimination.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Donnelly</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1025-f1" n="3" xml:id="d1025-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; the Chargé reported in this despatch that steps were being taken in
                    the Canal Zone to curtail contraband trade in merchandise sold by the
                    commissaries (811F.244/5–2245).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1025-f2" n="4" xml:id="d1025-f2-content">
                <p>A privilege extended to members of the so-called gold roll, or the skilled
                    employees of the Canal Zone.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
